   {
    "title": "Principal Engineer",
    "company": "Chef Software",
    "location": "Seattle",
    "description": "Developed multiple OSS products and projects in Erlang, Rust, Ruby and C, specializing in solving difficult optimization and scalability problems and distributed systems. Interviewed a good fraction of Chef's engineering hires growing the company while helping build a fantastic company culture. Mentored multiple SDE and interns from hiring through promotion to SDE3. Part of our Open Source community team, including public issue triages and PR review of multiple open source projects and assisting in meetups and other community building efforts. Lived the ``DevOps life'', including maintaining, deploying and troubleshooting both Chef Server and Builder SaaS systems. Served\nas highest tier of support for customer installs of our services, including fixing outages, finding root\ncauses, and providing both short term workarounds and long term fixes.\n\nProjects include:  \n* Habitat Builder, a Rust based SaaS API, content delivery, and build system. Implemented a graph based algorithm to compute package build orders in the presence of circular dependencies, along with a Tokio based asynchronous work scheduler to control remote build machines.\n*  Push Jobs Server, a remote execution service in Erlang and Ruby able to control 20k nodes via ZMQ.\n*  Chef Server Erlang implementation, a rewrite of our Ruby based SaaS product in Erlang, resulting in a 20x smaller memory footprint while scaling to Facebook class usage.\n*  Dep Selector: one of the first systems to apply a generalized constraint solver to the version resolution problem. Despite it being a NP-complete problem, found a viable problem subset where the solver was generally 50x faster than the database query feeding it data.\n",
